Taking shelter inside harmless vortices is a well-known late game
strategy. The big problems with this approach are that vortices move
erratically, and that other enemies can gang up on you in the
meantime.

So why is the castle strategy I posted "broken"? In Sporkhack's
castle, there's not much freedom of movement for a vortex at the
castle gate, so it *will* find its way though the bars. And enemies
can't gang up on you once you're inside. With locking or a key, you
only have to deal with a narrow corridor with five soldiers *max* and
have a 50/50 (far better with wand of probing) chance of snagging the
wand before facing the castle inhabitants.


